// @expect-fail: Error: matrix rows must have equal length
// @contract: C-358
// #2482: a ragged `from_lists` is not a matrix. Native stores a flat
// `rows * cols` buffer and its constructor asserted `data.len() == rows *
// cols` — a raw `assertion left == right failed` panic (exit 101) — while
// the wasm legs, whose Matrix is a list of rows with no shape invariant,
// built the ragged value and read on: the structural leg zero-filled the
// short row (`[[1, 2], [3, 0]]`) and the incumbent kept it short
// (`[[1, 2], [3]]`), so the two wasm legs did not even agree with each
// other. C-282 already stated that no public constructor builds a ragged
// matrix; this is the guard that makes the statement true.
fn main() -> Unit = {
  let m = matrix.from_lists([
    [1.0, 2.0],
    [3.0]
  ])
  println("UNREACHABLE ${matrix.rows(m)}x${matrix.cols(m)}")
}
